  "workload_notes": [
    "The duplicate burst synchronizes clients ahead of the tenant row lock. Before the fix the benchmark reproduced an erroneous rate-limit rejection instead of replaying the winning receipt.",
    "Queue latency starts after the client barrier and includes connection checkout, the SQL transaction and commit or rollback. With eight samples nearest-rank p95 is the slowest attempt.",
    "The per-file SST spans include disk read, SHA-256, validation and parsing. They dominate this run. Qualification and the prototype reduction with its internal validation are timed separately.",
    "SST peak uses tracemalloc and measures Python heap allocations during parsing, qualification and reduction. Process RSS and remote retrieval are outside this workload.",
    "The approved plan ledger values are reserved limits in USD. Actual billing and provider costs are outside this workload."
